# External Access Point Guardrail

External Access Point is **not** an AP configuration/provisioning feature.

Owner configures the AP in its own manufacturer web UI (AP/bridge, DHCP off, NAT off), plugs LAN into MikroTik, then registers the management IP in Renz-Fi. MikroTik remains DHCP/NAT/HotSpot/voucher/User Profile/rate-limit authority. The AP is Wi-Fi coverage + Layer-2 bridge only.

## Renz-Fi may

- Register metadata (name, management IP, optional credentials, SSID label, location, notes, brand label)
- Validate management IP against **live** Ethernet LAN
- Run generic reachability on `ap_check_worker` (ICMP + TCP 80/443, HTTP 202, single-flight)
- Show RAM status
- Open `http://{managementIp}` in the browser (no ESP32 proxy, no credential injection)

## Renz-Fi must not

- Log in to the AP or send stored username/password to the AP
- HTTP GET-with-auth / POST / PUT / PATCH / DELETE against the AP
- Change SSID, Wi-Fi password, DHCP, NAT, channel, TX power, VLAN, QoS, firmware, or reboot the AP
- Add TP-Link / Ruijie / Tenda / COMFAST / ASUS / Ubiquiti / MikroTik-AP / OpenWrt AP configuration drivers
- Treat `vendor` as a driver selector
- Add AP-side bandwidth / promo / rate-limit
- Add VLAN fields or AP VLAN provisioning
- Claim seamless roaming (same SSID is allowed)
- Put AP checks on RouterWorker / MikroTikDriver / RouterOsClient / async_tcp / loopTask
- Read or write SD / take STORAGE_LOCK during a check
- Run automatic high-frequency or LAN-scan monitoring
- Merge this feature with `ManagementApManager` (ESP32 SoftAP at 192.168.4.1)

`GenericApDriver` is a **reachability probe**, not a configuration driver. Credentials are metadata only.

Source of truth: `docs/EXTERNAL_ACCESS_POINT_ARCHITECTURE.md`.
Do not move `v0.5.0-fully-operational`. Do not rewrite Stage B/C checkpoints.
